{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RenderingServer\/ViewportScaling3DMode\/fsr"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RenderingServer","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RenderingServer\/ViewportScaling3DMode"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fsr"}],"symbolKind":"case","title":"RenderingServer.ViewportScaling3DMode.fsr","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Case","modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot15RenderingServerC21ViewportScaling3DModeO3fsryA2EmF"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use AMD FidelityFX Super Resolution 1.0 upscaling for the viewport’s 3D buffer. The amount of scaling can be set using "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Viewport\/scaling3dScale","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Values less than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.0"},{"type":"text","text":" will be result in the viewport being upscaled using FSR. Values greater than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.0"},{"type":"text","text":" are not supported and bilinear downsampling will be used instead. A value of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.0"},{"type":"text","text":" disables scaling."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/renderingserver\/viewportscaling3dmode\/fsr"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fsr"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/RenderingServer":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RenderingServer","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RenderingServer","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"RenderingServer","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RenderingServer","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Server for anything visible.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/renderingserver","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Framework to write Godot Game Extensions using the Swift Programming Language."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","title":"SwiftGodot","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Viewport/scaling3dScale":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Scales the 3D render buffer based on the viewport size uses an image filter specified in "},{"code":"ProjectSettings\/rendering\/scaling3d\/mode","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to scale the output image to the full viewport size. Values lower than "},{"code":"1.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can be used to speed up 3D rendering at the cost of quality (undersampling). Values greater than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.0"},{"type":"text","text":" are only valid for bilinear mode and can be used to improve 3D rendering quality at a high performance cost (supersampling). See also "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProjectSettings\/rendering\/antiAliasing\/quality\/msaa3d"},{"type":"text","text":" for multi-sample antialiasing, which is significantly cheaper but only smooths the edges of polygons."}],"type":"topic","title":"scaling3dScale","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/viewport\/scaling3dscale","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"scaling3dScale"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"}],"kind":"symbol","identif